  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::26251",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with potassium channels through a shared mechanism involving the delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6, Kcnv2, and Kcna7, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, and this activity is associated with Kcng2. This indicates that Guanidine may influence Kcng2 through a common pathway involving potassium channel function. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with Guanidine potentially modulating Kcng2 via its effect on potassium channel activity. The overlapping roles of these potassium channels in delayed rectifier function imply that Guanidine may exert its effects on Kcng2 through a mechanism that involves the regulation of potassium channel activity, which is a key component of cellular electrophysiology.",
